index 613c631b12..4561e2ad5f 100644
--- a/ops/changelog.md
+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -9343,3 +9343,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE A1 (ARC NORTH STAR; PRIMARY; operator MANDATORY #1 lever; verifier_is_oracle=true) -- Config/toggle game SOLVE via verifier-GROUNDED win-RULE induction. .407 added 0 reproducible levels because static per-mechanic unit tests document blockers but do not deepen ARC. The freshest, validated, operator-hands-on lever (docs/research-notes/arc-config-layerb-scaffolded-2026-06-18.md): a local offline gemma-4-12B that CANNOT read a raw 64x64 scene CAN induce a GROUNDED relational win-RULE when handed object-centric digests (ka59 reached Tier-2 count_4==32, fires-on-win, 0 false-positives), and the verifier GROUNDS/REJECTS the proposed predicate (propose-then-ground). The operator's first-contact audit names the 9 toggle/CONFIG games (bp35, dc22, g50t, ka59, lf52, s5i5, tn36, sc25, tr87) as 'the clear #1 next investment and the genuinely hard one' -- target-PATTERN (win-rule) induction over a 40-210-cell editable space random exploration cannot stumble. THE STEP: REUSE the validated scaffolded inducer (scripts/experiments/arc3_config_layerb_scaffolded.py) -- object-centric digest (editable bbox + value counts; reference connected-component features, NEVER a raw grid) -> local gemma-12B-Q4 on the iGPU proposes is_win(grid) -> the verifier GROUNDS it on the banked win + non-wins -> wire the grounded predicate as the OfflineSolver verifier (arc_solver_kit) to drive a best-first search to the NEXT level. Targets (per-game checkpoint + wall-time cap; breadth beats all-or-nothing): ka59 L2 (rule known -> drive the solve) + FIRST-CONTACT win-rule grounding on >=2 UNSOLVED config games (bp35/dc22/g50t/lf52/s5i5). HARD gate per target: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior reproduced best (arc_solver_kit.reproduce) OR a Tier-2 GROUNDED win-rule for a NEW config game (honest partial -- the rule grounds; the search-to-win is the logged residual). verifier_is_oracle=true (the SOLVE is execution-grounded -- ARC progress, NOT an oracle-distinct moat headline; the contribution is that the verifier GROUNDS the LLM-proposed rule). The local gemma-12B runs on the iGPU ONLY (never the 3090s), offline-legal, zero quota. NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH target. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_config_rule_partial; results/experiment_4414_config_rule_induction_solve.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE A2 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY; flagged_for_v408; verifier_is_oracle=true) -- Agent2World ADAPTIVE E3 mechanic repair (arXiv:2512.22336, the .407 SOTA-ingestion flagged_for_v408) + AERA speed-depth/leakage controls (arXiv:2605.25931) on the deep-tail games where .407 STATIC per-mechanic unit tests passed but reproduction did NOT follow: ar25 L2 + tn36 L8 + lp85 L6, +1 each per Incremental-Progress Scoping. .407 (exp4405/4406) wrote STATIC per-mechanic unit tests, passed them (ar25 register test 1.0), and STILL produced 0 new reproducible levels (lookahead_fidelity stuck ~0.73 -- the named registers are not the whole gap). STATED forward difference (Agent2World): a 'Testing Team' generates ADAPTIVE, behavior-aware tests FROM the failing K-step rollout traces (not a fixed list of named-register tests), feeds the failing traces to the world-model developer, and reruns executable simulation checks BEFORE any solve -- so the tests track the ACTUAL mismatched transitions the model still gets wrong, round over round. AERA controls: keep held-out mechanic tests + fresh-agent state + solve-claims SEPARATE from test repair (no benchmark/public-artifact leakage). The codex agent IS the world-model developer (NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per game: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior best (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). An honest partial per game (the adaptive tests that now PASS + the residual failing-behavior test as the sharper world-model gap CLASS) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_adaptive_partial; results/experiment_4415_agent2world_adaptive_e3_repair.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE B1 (ORACLE-DISTINCT FRONTIER; operator P0; DEFINITIVE FALSIFICATION; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- Hidden-state first-error localization AUDIT (arXiv:2605.13772 GeoReason hidden-state transport, the .407 SOTA-ingestion method). The TEXT first-error localizer is RETIRED (.407 exp4403: on FoVer the content-blind POSITION-ONLY baseline F1=1.0 -- first-error onset is near-deterministic in POSITION, ~zero CONTENT headroom in text; the real-intervention localizer tied it, delta_vs_position_only=0.0; retire_if_same_verdict fired). This is the ONE remaining oracle-distinct first-error question worth a SINGLE bounded shot: does the signal exist OFF-TEXT -- does a model HIDDEN-STATE transport margin carry ANY recoverable NON-position first-error signal that text position alone does not? A DIAGNOSTIC FALSIFICATION (NOT a redeployable localizer): (1) capture per-step hidden states from a LOCAL open model over the cached FoVer step-labeled traces; (2) compute a hidden-state transport/margin feature per step; (3) compare its first-error localization F1 against the content-blind position-only baseline on a held-out split, n>=1000. Emit hidden_state_localizer_has_nonposition_signal BARE bool := (the hidden-state localizer beats the position-only baseline, delta CI95-excl-0). A CLEAN NULL conclusively CLOSES the entire first-error-localizer program (text AND hidden-state both position-bound -- do not revisit). A weak signal is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (the off-text discriminator), NOT redeployed as a headline. verifier_is_oracle=false (a learned probe over hidden states; the reference prefix-check defines correctness). Cached corpus; the hidden-state capture is a single bounded forward pass; NO live training, NO generator SFT, NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: clean_powered_null_position_only_not_beaten; results/experiment_4416_hidden_state_localizer_falsification_audit.json
+- 2026-06-19: PHASE B2 (verifier-earns-its-place; SOVEREIGNTY tier; verifier_is_oracle=true) -- GAP-4 rule-execution verifier with a LOCAL open-weight generator arm + a graded execution-energy gate (the GAP-4 forward protocol's decentralization tier, ops/verifier_gaps.md GAP-4). The GAP-4 rule-execution verifier (induce def transform(grid) from demos, demo-perfect program reranks the TRM pool) landed a positive on ARC-1 with codex/gpt-5.5, but it is contaminated (30/31 tasks in public training) AND the generator is closed (a decentralization gap -- CLAUDE.md Rule 1). north-star §5's win-condition is the verifier earning its place. THE STEP: re-run the GAP-4 gate with a LOCAL open-weight generator (Gemma-4/Qwen3.6 GGUF, cached) as the program inducer + the graded min-hamming gate (tau=0.005, vote-aware guard) + k-consistency agreement, and measure pass@2 on the cached TRM rerank pool vs the matched no-verifier (vote) control. .407-prior local-MoE attempts (exp4069) found a local generator surfaced demo-perfect programs at only ~0.23 coverage; STATED forward difference: the graded execution-energy gate (tau-relaxed near-miss promotion) + k-consistency agreement + a stronger/cached candidate pool, measuring the GATE's pass@2 effect (not just raw coverage). Emit sovereign_gap4_gate_holds BARE bool := (a LOCAL-generator demo-fit gate holds pass@2 >= vote with 0 pass@2 losses on the matched pool, CI95). verifier_is_oracle=true (the execution gate IS the oracle -- this is the SOVEREIGNTY/decentralization question, NOT an oracle-distinct moat headline). A clean null (the local generator cannot drive the gate) is LOGGED as a decentralization gap (the product backlog). Cached pool + cached GGUF; CPU/iGPU; NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: sovereign_gap4_local_gate_holds_flat_cov_0.2333_fires_0_lost_0; results/experiment_4417_gap4_local_generator_sovereign_arm.json
